    name: 'durin-hooks',
    content:
      "---\nname: durin-hooks\ndescription: Configure or diagnose Durin local pre-tool hooks for a coding harness, an installed Endpoint helper, or a custom checker.\n---\n\nLocal hooks run before supported harness tool calls. They are cooperative\nchecks, separate from Durin's gateway authorization and independent approvals.\n\nRun `npx @accessdurin/cli hooks status` to inspect the saved hook installation.\nUse interactive `npx @accessdurin/cli` to configure the selected harness, its\nskills, and its local checker. Built-in adapters cover Claude Code, Codex,\nCursor, Windsurf, OpenCode, Gemini CLI, and GitHub Copilot CLI. Other harnesses use a custom descriptor and must\ninvoke the documented stdin hook contract before execution.\n\nA checker must be an explicitly selected executable. Existing Endpoint helpers accept Claude/Codex events only; use a compatible custom checker for other harnesses. Endpoint helpers evaluate\nlocally using Endpoint's policy pack; a custom checker receives the normalized\nPreToolUse JSON object on stdin and returns 0 to continue or 2 to deny. Missing\nhelpers, invalid input, checker errors, and timeouts are reported as failures.\nDo not replace a real checker with a command that always succeeds.\n\nPreserve unrelated hooks and settings. Do not clear `disableAllHooks` or bypass\na harness trust prompt. Reopen the agent after setup and review Codex hooks in\n`/hooks`. Configuration alone does not establish that the harness executed it.\n\nTool arguments go to the local checker. These hooks do not independently upload\ntool inputs to a new Durin API. Endpoint organization reporting uses its own\nenrollment and platform capabilities; gateway calls use the selected MCP grant.\n",
